2. The standard enthalpy change for the reaction (from Step 5) is \(\Delta H^\circ_{\text{rxn}} = -300.79 \, \text{kJ}\).

3. Using the equation from Step 4 for the formation enthalpies:
   \[ \Delta H^\circ_{\text{rxn}} = 2\Delta H^\circ_f(\text{HgO}(s)) - 2\Delta H^\circ_f(\text{Hg}(g)) - \Delta H^\circ_f(\text{O}_2(g)) \]

